    "finish_elapsed_s": 9.599784586054739,
    "text": "A refrigerator works by moving heat, not by making \"cold.\" A special liquid called refrigerant flows through pipes. First, it passes through a compressor that squeezes it, making it hot. That heat escapes through coils on the back or bottom of the fridge. Then the refrigerant expands, becoming very cold. As it flows through pipes inside the fridge, it absorbs heat from your food and air. Finally, it travels back to the compressor to start again. A thermostat senses the temperature and turns the compressor on or off to keep things just right. So your fridge is really a heat mover, pumping warmth out so the inside stays chilly!"
  }
